From 964e27f3ec97204eee4d0ebb2cc55fe1ebc7d0aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEGIS Platform Team <aegis-ops@localhost>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:03:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P4 runtime caps + command-target parsing: survive the capped
 engagement container (PILOT-02 rounds)

Two engagement-container findings from the first completed live
run (PILOT-02, replay OK / SLO 7/7 PASS):

#4 nmap present but NOT EXECUTABLE (EPERM for every user, root
   included). Root cause: Kali ships /usr/lib/nmap/nmap with file
   caps cap_net_bind_service,cap_net_admin,cap_net_raw; the compose
   cap_drop:ALL + cap_add:NET_RAW,NET_ADMIN leaves cap_net_bind_service
   outside the process bounding set, and execve refuses any binary
   whose file caps exceed it (the sh wrapper surfaces rc=127
   "Operation not permitted"). Fixes: compose cap_add gains
   NET_BIND_SERVICE; the Dockerfile normalizes the binary to
   cap_net_admin,cap_net_raw=eip (step 1b; libcap2-bin joins the apt
   set); doctor probe-execs every runtime attachment so a
   present-but-dead binary can never pass pre-flight silently again
   (soft WARN, matching the optional-runtime doctrine). The
   no-new-privileges comment now warns that enabling it would block
   file-cap acquisition at exec.

#5 scope-parser false positives denied 6 in-scope-intent commands in
   PILOT-02 (the model worked around each within a turn).
   extract_targets_from_command now: (a) drops IP/nnn tokens not in
   argument position (URL/path suffixes -- "curl http://10.10.0.5/22":
   the host still gates via the URL/bare-IP tokens); (b) drops IP/nnn
   suffixes over 32 (never a prefix length -- host/port or path
   notation); (c) keeps argument-position CIDRs STRICT, sloppy
   host-bits-set notation included ("nmap 10.10.0.5/22" is
   network-scan intent under nmap semantics -- deny-by-default wins);
   (d) skips domain-shaped tokens in path position ("python3
   ws/probe.py", "nmap -iL /tmp/hosts.txt"); (e) extends
   _CODE_ATTR_SUFFIXES with exception attrs (socket.timeout) and
   never-delegated file extensions -- deliberately NOT py/sh/md (real
   ccTLDs: bare host targets stay gated).

Security posture: both fixes tighten or preserve deny-by-default; the
only loosened behaviors are the two demonstrated false-positive shapes,
where the actual connection target continues to be gated by its own
extracted token. tests/test_permissions.py +9, tests/test_doctor.py
new (6).
